{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27259464","formula":"C₄H₈O₃S","hill":"C4H8O3S","elements":["H","C","O","S"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":8.0,"O":3.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"1,4-butanesultone"},"descriptions":{"en":"1,4-butane sultone is a six-membered δ-sultone and the cyclic ester of 4-hydroxybutanesulfonic acid. As a sulfo-alkylating agent, 1,4-butanesultone is used to introduce the sulfobutyl group (–(CH2)4–SO3−) into hydrophobic compounds possessing nucleophilic functional groups, for example hydroxy groups (as in the case of β-cyclodextrin) or amino groups (as in the case of polymethine dyes). In such, the sulfobutyl group is present as neutral sodium salt and considerably increases the water solubility of the derivatives."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":15411,"mass":136.17,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CCS(=O)(=O)OC1","inchikey":"MHYFEEDKONKGEB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oxathiane 2,2-dioxide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"15411","atoms":16,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.079,"y":0.001,"z":0.048,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.084,"y":-1.206,"z":-0.427,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.231,"y":0.023,"z":-0.832,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.229,"y":-0.03,"z":1.488,"el":"O"},{"x":1.372,"y":1.22,"z":0.209,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.017,"y":1.364,"z":-0.396,"el":"C"},{"x":2.049,"y":-0.076,"z":-0.232,"el":"C"},{"x":1.219,"y":-1.297,"z":0.142,"el":"C"},{"x":1.307,"y":1.242,"z":1.303,"el":"H"},{"x":1.989,"y":2.074,"z":-0.094,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.502,"y":2.278,"z":-0.042,"el":"H"},{"x":0.031,"y":1.398,"z":-1.489,"el":"H"},{"x":2.183,"y":-0.05,"z":-1.321,"el":"H"},{"x":3.043,"y":-0.15,"z":0.221,"el":"H"},{"x":1.692,"y":-2.203,"z":-0.248,"el":"H"},{"x":1.137,"y":-1.406,"z":1.229,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,2],[0,3,2],[0,5,1],[1,7,1],[4,5,1],[4,6,1],[4,8,1],[4,9,1],[5,10,1],[5,11,1],[6,7,1],[6,12,1],[6,13,1],[7,14,1],[7